    "mechanism": "hls.js attaches through MSE, so the media element has no resource of its own to load and the mode the captions_default effect set is never disturbed. Native HLS points <video src> at the master playlist, so the element runs its own load AFTER that effect, attaches the stream's in-band text tracks and comes back with every mode reset. components/player/VideoPlayer.tsx applied once and latched, so the reset was final.",
    "fix": "vidra-user #215 — re-assert on the element's own load milestones and on a text-track list change, and stop as soon as the viewer operates the captions control.",
    "tdd": "RED first: the re-apply test failed against the unpatched effect (expected 'disabled' to be 'showing'); a third test pins the don't-fight-the-viewer half."
  },
