  "not_proven": [
    "Physical speaker output. Safari 26.5 exposes no webkitAudioDecodedByteCount, and a MediaElementSource tap on a natively-played HLS element reads RMS 0 in WebKit regardless of sound, so the audible-track clause rests on the audio rendition's segments arriving, one enabled audio track, unmuted at full volume, and the source tone decoding to peak 0.153 off /original.",
    "iOS Safari. The MSE-partial Apple browser the A07/A08 carry-in was really about was not driven; this is desktop Safari with both MSE spellings removed.",
    "Anything at a CDN edge or behind presign. Every byte came from the api through the loopback proxy (delivery_source api-proxy on every beacon).",
    "A cold-cache Safari fallback. Safari's own progressive-fallback attempt kept playing a cached master; the fallback measured here is the one taken by the native engine after the master 404'd on a fresh mount.",
    "Live and federated surfaces. This is VOD only."
  ]
